    "detail": [
      "cargo-deny requires its toolchain action and action rust-version input to agree; deny policy and full scan scope stay unchanged.",
      "rust-ci-full-nextest-platform requires both archive and shard compilers to agree.",
      "v8-canary and rusty-v8-release include direct cargo +VERSION invocations; v8-canary also locates an absolute cargo executable by toolchain directory.",
      "hepta-offline-build-inputs packages a compiler distribution and sets RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN; all selectors and packaging paths must agree.",
      "hepta-lane-e-gap-closure records tooling.rust in a produced evidence manifest; the recorded version must track the actual compiler.",
      "Only stable jobs in mixed stable/nightly workflow files migrate; the independently compiled nightly lint plugin remains nightly."
    ]
  },
